OL,3,GNEWSAIsland Energy: No plans to remove
OL,4,Agas standing charge
OL,5,
OL,6,FIsland Energy said any proposed changes
OL,7,Fwould be subject to consultation with
OL,8,Fthe Communications and and Utilities
OL,9,FRegulatory Authority (CURA) on the
OL,10,Fisland.
OL,12,FA spokesperson warned removing standing
OL,13,Fcharges may benefit some customers but
OL,14,Fcould see others pay more.
